":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Bug Description\n\nThe SKILL.md YAML frontmatter validator in VS Code Copilot reports a warning for the `allowed-tools` attribute, even though it is a valid field defined in the [Agent Skills specification](https://agentskills.io/specification#allowed-tools-field).\n\n## Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Create or open a `SKILL.md` with `allowed-tools` in the YAML frontmatter.\n2. Observe the warning.\n\n## Actual Behavior\n\n> Attribute 'allowed-tools' is not supported in skill files.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\n`allowed-tools` should be recognized as valid per the Agent Skills spec.\n\n## Environment\n\n- VS Code Insiders\n- GitHub Copilot extension (latest)\n- Windows 11","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/14131/reactions","total_count":6,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/14131/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null},"comments":[]}